# The file where `M227` `D` (`D1235`) is visible by hand — the footer yielding to a live playback.
#
# **It has to be ONE file, and that is not a convenience.** `ComposeDoor` clears the played test on
# a change of PATH, not of line (`useEffect(() => setPlayed(null), [path])`), so pressing ▶ in one
# file and then opening the workload test in another resets the stage to `empty` and the footer
# comes straight back — you would see the before state twice and never the after. Every other file
# in this directory is workload-only, and `browser-contrast.tflw` is browser-only, so before this
# one there was nowhere in the corpus the two facts could be true at once.
#
# **The two tests cannot be one test** (`D1205`): a workload may not sit beside a browser step, so
# what the file carries is a playable browser test and a workload-bearing api test, the way
# `browser-contrast.tflw` already carries a browser test and an api one.
#
# By hand, on the BROWSER door:
#
#   1. select `the catalogue holds up as readers arrive` — region 2 is the page's full width,
#      spanning the sequence column, with the plan in it (`D1225`).
#   2. press ▶ on `a page to play, so the stage has something in it`, and wait for the trace.
#   3. select the workload test again — region 2 is back in the editor column, and the playback
#      region is the only full-width band on the page (`D1235`).
#
# **Needs the storefront up as well as the api** — `node cli.mjs start` brings both; the page is
# webV2's nginx on :8090, and `traceViewer` has to be true for step 2 to produce anything.

@ui
test "a page to play, so the stage has something in it"
  open "/"
  expect text "Browse all products (windowed list)" is visible

@catalogue @workload
test "the catalogue holds up as readers arrive"
  ramp to 5 users over 2s
  api GET /products
  expect status equals 200
  threshold error rate is less than 5%
